    {
      "page_title": "Why Consumer Groups Exist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What A Group Is",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Group = consumers sharing one `group.id`",
            "They split a topic's partitions cooperatively",
            "Invariant: one partition, one consumer, never two",
            "One consumer may own many partitions",
            "Change `group.id` and it is a brand-new group"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Parallelism Ceiling"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Max useful consumers = partition count",
            "Extras sit idle with zero assignment",
            "Adding partitions raises the ceiling",
            "Partitions can never be removed from a topic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "p0 c0",
              "p1 c1",
              "p2 c2",
              "p3 c3",
              "p4 c4",
              "p5 c5",
              "idle c6",
              "idle c7"
            ],
            "caption": "6 partitions, 8 consumers"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fan-Out vs Queue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Same `group.id`",
                "lines": [
                  "Work is split",
                  "Queue semantics",
                  "Each record once"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Other `group.id`",
                "lines": [
                  "Full copy of stream",
                  "Topic semantics",
                  "pub/sub fan-out"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ordering Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ordering is guaranteed per partition only",
            "No total order across a topic",
            "Keyed records hash to a fixed partition",
            "So one key stays ordered under one consumer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Coordinator + Health"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Coordinator = broker owning the group's `__consumer_offsets` partition",
            "Chosen by `hash(group.id) % partitions`",
            "States: Empty, PreparingRebalance, CompletingRebalance",
            "Then Stable, and Dead when gone"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-consumer-groups.sh \\",
            "  --bootstrap-server b:9092 \\",
            "  --describe --group orders",
            "# members, offsets, lag"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Column",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "CURRENT-OFFSET",
              "committed"
            ],
            [
              "LOG-END-OFFSET",
              "tip of partition"
            ],
            [
              "LAG",
              "end minus current"
            ],
            [
              "CONSUMER-ID",
              "member owning it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "consumer.commitSync(Map.of(tp,",
            "  new OffsetAndMetadata(",
            "    lastOffset + 1)));",
            "// explicit, per-partition, mid-batch"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Why Consumer Groups Exist (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Lag is the metric",
          "text": "Lag = log-end offset minus committed offset. Track it before CPU, before memory."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Scaling myth",
          "items": [
            "12 consumers on 6 partitions = 6 idle",
            "Throughput does not double",
            "Repartition, or shrink the fleet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Join Dance",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "FindCoordinator",
              "JoinGroup",
              "leader assigns",
              "SyncGroup",
              "Heartbeat"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "FindCoordinator: ask any broker who owns the group",
            "JoinGroup: send strategies plus subscription",
            "Coordinator names one member group leader",
            "SyncGroup: leader uploads the full assignment map",
            "Coordinator fans out each member's slice"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Computes What"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The leader is a consumer, not a broker",
            "Assignment logic runs client-side",
            "Leader sees the whole subscription picture",
            "So custom assignors can be rack- or load-aware"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Heartbeats + Fencing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Background thread pings the coordinator to prove liveness",
            "It is also how a consumer learns a rebalance started",
            "`member.id` is coordinator-assigned per session",
            "Restart gets a new one, unless static membership"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "JoinGroup #1 -> MEMBER_ID_REQUIRED",
            "JoinGroup #2 (carries member.id) -> ok",
            "# forced registration blocks join storms"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`generation.id` increments on every rebalance",
            "Stale-generation requests are rejected outright",
            "That is how zombie consumers get fenced"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Membership: Join, Sync, Heartbeat",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Coordinator Failover"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A dead coordinator triggers a rebalance too. It fires once the `__consumer_offsets` partition leader moves to a new broker."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "KIP-848 + Metrics"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "KIP-848 moves assignment onto the broker",
            "No client-side leader, no stop-the-world sync",
            "Watch `rebalance-rate-per-hour`",
            "Watch `rebalance-latency-avg`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two joins that hurt",
          "items": [
            "Members sharing no common assignment strategy fail the join",
            "Different topics under one `group.id`",
            "Mixed subscriptions rebalance together and thrash"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What A Rebalance Is",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The group re-deciding who owns which partition. Correctness-safe, availability-hostile."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Five Triggers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trigger",
            "Detected by"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "New member joins",
              "JoinGroup"
            ],
            [
              "Graceful `close()`",
              "LeaveGroup"
            ],
            [
              "Heartbeat gap",
              "`session.timeout.ms`"
            ],
            [
              "Processing gap",
              "`max.poll.interval.ms`"
            ],
            [
              "Partition count change",
              "metadata refresh"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scale-up, restart and deploy all count as joins",
            "A regex subscription matching a new topic also fires",
            "Trigger 5 needs no member change at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Eager = Stop The World"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every member revokes every partition",
            "The whole group re-joins, consumption fully stalls",
            "Stall = detect + join wait + assign + state restore",
            "Stateful apps measure that in minutes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "revoke all",
              "re-join",
              "assign",
              "restore state",
              "resume"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Rebalancing: Triggers and Cost",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Listener Contract"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Callback",
            "What to do"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`onPartitionsRevoked`",
              "commit offsets here"
            ],
            [
              "`onPartitionsAssigned`",
              "seek, restore state"
            ],
            [
              "`onPartitionsLost`",
              "do NOT commit"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`onPartitionsLost` fires when fenced or timed out",
            "Ownership is already gone there",
            "A commit would clobber the new owner's progress",
            "Commit on revoke or duplicates are guaranteed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Storms"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Rolling restart of N consumers: up to N rebalances",
            "Eager churn scales worse than linear",
            "Cascading: slow member times out mid-rebalance, re-joins, repeats",
            "`group.initial.rebalance.delay.ms` (default 3000) batches startup joins"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Minimize count, not duration",
          "text": "Rebalances never lose correctness, they lose availability. Design so they rarely happen."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking An Assignor",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`partition.assignment.strategy` is an ordered class list",
            "The group picks the highest strategy common to all",
            "Kafka 4.x default: `[RangeAssignor, CooperativeStickyAssignor]`",
            "Set cooperative-sticky explicitly to actually get it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "p.put(\"partition.assignment.strategy\",",
            "  CooperativeStickyAssignor.class",
            "    .getName());  // opt in",
            "// modern default choice"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Range"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Per topic, sorts partitions and consumers",
            "Hands out contiguous ranges",
            "3 partitions, 2 consumers: consumer-0 gets the extra",
            "Skew compounds across every subscribed topic",
            "Upside: `topic-A-p0` and `topic-B-p0` land together"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "A-p0 c0",
              "A-p1 c0",
              "A-p2 c1",
              "B-p0 c0",
              "B-p1 c0",
              "B-p2 c1"
            ],
            "caption": "Range, 3p per topic"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Assignment Strategies Compared",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "RoundRobin + Sticky"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RoundRobin flattens all partitions of all topics",
            "Deals them one by one: best raw balance",
            "Flaw: any membership change reshuffles nearly everything",
            "Sticky balances the same but keeps prior owners",
            "CooperativeSticky = sticky plus incremental protocol"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Side By Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Range",
            "RoundRobin",
            "Coop-Sticky"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Balance",
              "worst",
              "best",
              "best"
            ],
            [
              "Movement",
              "high",
              "high",
              "low"
            ],
            [
              "Co-partition",
              "yes",
              "no",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "Blocking",
              "yes",
              "yes",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Balance quality",
          "text": "RoundRobin, Sticky and CooperativeSticky tie; Range trails. Range only wins on co-partitioned local joins."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Escape Hatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Custom: extend `AbstractPartitionAssignor`",
            "Rack-aware, weighted or cost-based placement",
            "`assign()` bypasses groups: no rebalance, no coordinator",
            "With `assign()` you own placement and failover"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Switching strategies live",
          "items": [
            "Never flip a whole fleet in one deploy",
            "Two-phase rolling deploy only",
            "Members must always share one strategy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Goal",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stop the world only for partitions that actually move",
            "Protocol version bumps EAGER to COOPERATIVE",
            "Switch is `CooperativeStickyAssignor`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Incremental Cooperative Rebalancing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Rounds"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "rejoin, keep all",
              "leader targets",
              "revoke deltas",
              "second rebalance",
              "new owners"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Round 1: everyone rejoins holding their partitions",
            "Leader computes the target, revokes only deltas",
            "Round 2 follows at once, handing them over",
            "Two rebalances per change, no full stall",
            "Untouched partitions keep polling throughout"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Streams gains most",
          "text": "Long state-restore apps stop rebuilding every state store on every scale event."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Migration Is Strict"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Deploy",
            "Strategy list"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "`[CooperativeSticky, Eager]`"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "`[CooperativeSticky]`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Skipping phase 1 mixes protocols in one group",
            "Result: `IllegalStateException` or broken assignments",
            "Both rolls must complete before the next change"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Callbacks Change"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`onPartitionsRevoked` gets only the moved partitions",
            "Not the full set, the way eager did",
            "`onPartitionsLost` finally becomes meaningful",
            "It separates clean handoff from fencing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Static Membership"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`group.instance.id` gives a pod a stable identity",
            "Restart inside `session.timeout.ms` causes NO rebalance",
            "Complementary to cooperative mode, not a substitute",
            "Set the timeout above pod restart time, 45s to 5min",
            "Too high and real failure detection lags"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-consumer-groups.sh \\",
            "  --delete-offsets --group orders",
            "# or admin removeMembersFrom",
            "#   ConsumerGroup for scale-down"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Incremental Cooperative Rebalancing (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Duplicate instance id",
          "items": [
            "Two live pods, one `group.instance.id`",
            "One is fenced with FencedInstanceIdException",
            "Derive it from the StatefulSet ordinal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What An Offset Is",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Per-partition, monotonically increasing message index",
            "Not a timestamp, not global",
            "Committed offset = the NEXT offset to read",
            "That is last processed + 1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "long last = record.offset();  // 41",
            "commit(tp, new OffsetAndMetadata(",
            "  last + 1));                 // 42",
            "// off-by-one here replays forever"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where They Live"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Internal compacted topic `__consumer_offsets`",
            "50 partitions by default",
            "Keyed by (group, topic, partition)",
            "Compaction keeps only the latest value per key",
            "So the offsets topic stays bounded"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Number",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`position()`",
              "next record read"
            ],
            [
              "`committed()`",
              "last durably stored"
            ],
            [
              "log-end offset",
              "tip of partition"
            ],
            [
              "high watermark",
              "on all in-sync replicas"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`position()` and `committed()` diverge in flight",
            "Consumers can only read below the high watermark",
            "Commits are per-partition maps",
            "So a partial commit is possible and normal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Moving On Purpose"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`seek(tp, offset)`, `seekToBeginning()`, `seekToEnd()`",
            "Valid only once an assignment exists",
            "`offsetsForTimes()` maps wall clock to first offset at or after",
            "That is the basis for time-travel replay"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kafka-consumer-groups.sh --reset-offsets \\",
            "  --to-earliest --group g --topic t \\",
            "  --execute   # group must be inactive"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Retention Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`offsets.retention.minutes` defaults to 7 days",
            "A fully inactive group loses its offsets",
            "Then `auto.offset.reset` decides everything"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "`auto.offset.reset`",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`earliest`",
              "replay from start"
            ],
            [
              "`latest`",
              "skip all before now"
            ],
            [
              "`none`",
              "NoOffsetForPartition"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Offsets are per group",
          "text": "A typo in `group.id` silently gives a full replay or a full skip. Nothing errors."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Committing: Auto, Sync, Async",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Auto-Commit",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`enable.auto.commit=true` is the default",
            "Commits the last poll's offsets on a timer inside `poll()`",
            "`auto.commit.interval.ms` defaults to 5000",
            "It commits what poll RETURNED, not what you PROCESSED",
            "A crash mid-batch loses those records"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Feels safe, is at-most-once",
          "text": "Relative to processing, auto-commit gives at-most-once. The default is the risky setting."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sync vs Async"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "`commitSync()`",
                "lines": [
                  "Blocks",
                  "Retries retriable errors",
                  "Throws on failure",
                  "End of batch, shutdown"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "`commitAsync()`",
                "lines": [
                  "Fire and forget",
                  "Optional callback",
                  "No retry",
                  "Higher throughput"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`commitAsync()` takes an `OffsetCommitCallback`",
            "Never blindly retry it",
            "A late retry of an old offset overwrites a newer commit",
            "Consequence: silent replay"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Canonical Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "while (running) {",
            "  process(consumer.poll(D));",
            "  consumer.commitAsync();  // hot loop",
            "}",
            "// finally: commitSync(); close();"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Delivery Semantics"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Want",
            "Do"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "At-most-once",
              "commit before processing"
            ],
            [
              "At-least-once",
              "commit after processing"
            ],
            [
              "Exactly-once",
              "transactions or DB offsets"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "At-least-once is the practical default",
            "Assume duplicates, make consumers idempotent",
            "Dedupe key, upsert, or an idempotency table"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Exactly-Once Wiring"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Producer `sendOffsetsToTransaction()` binds writes and offsets",
            "Consumer needs `isolation.level=read_committed`",
            "Such a consumer cannot read past the Last Stable Offset",
            "An open transaction stalls that partition's reads",
            "Kafka to SQL: store offsets in your own DB transaction"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Your consumer group is not slow because Kafka is slow — it is slow because it keeps rebalancing. 10 pages on how partitions get assigned, why the poll loop is really a heartbeat, what a committed offset actually means (last processed + 1), and the exact configs that turn a 45-second stall into an instant handoff. Save it for the next CommitFailedException.",
